<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <OutputType>Exe</OutputType>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <!-- LatestMajor, not LatestMinor: type providers erase to the analyzed
         project's RUNTIME references, and a net8 host handed lib/net10.0
         SQLProvider assemblies cannot instantiate them ("SqlDataProvider is
         not defined" on a project that builds cleanly). Running on the
         newest installed runtime lets the tool typecheck projects that
         target it; machines with only net8 still run on net8. -->
    <RollForward>LatestMajor</RollForward>
    <!-- ships as a dotnet tool: dotnet tool install fsharp-refactor -->
    <IsPackable>true</IsPackable>
    <PackAsTool>true</PackAsTool>
    <ToolCommandName>fsharp-refactor</ToolCommandName>
    <PackageId>fsharp-refactor</PackageId>
    <Description>Applies the FSharp.Refactor analyzers' quick fixes to F# code from the command line. Point it at a project, a script, a solution, a directory or a glob; --dry-run reports without editing. The tool clarifies the (agent-generated or old) code's intent, reduces non-alphanumeric noise, and uses built-in .NET libraries more efficiently.</Description>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>0.8.51: A run that fails or is interrupted (Ctrl+C) puts back the compilation in progress; a source that cannot be written costs that compilation, not a crash. A fsharprefactor.json that is no JSON, a --report into a missing directory, `--report --dry-run` and filters that leave no rule are refused before anything is written. A glob searches the directories it names (`src/App*/*.fsproj` swept all of `src`). A single named file gets no --api-changes reshapes. --mcp works inside the directory it is given or started in and writes nothing outside it, applies nothing under --dry-run, validates `codes` and `categories` and survives a malformed request. Prose such as "types generated by JsonProvider" no longer marks a file generated.

 0.8.50: FR0029&apos;s return hoist no longer takes the `elif` links after an awaiting arm as a branch of their own: it put `return` in front of the `elif` keyword, which didn&apos;t compile, and the build check rolled the edit back.

 0.8.49: FR0016 and FR0070 read what takes reference types only (a value, a record literal or a type argument given to it), in the project&apos;s other files and, under --api-changes, the projects referencing the type: [&lt;Struct&gt;] stopped TryAddSingleton compiling.

 0.8.48: New rules FR0183, and FR0184 (off by default): secrets and clients a redirect exposes. New rule FR0185 (off by default): unions with no fields can be structs. FR0016, FR0070, FR0130, FR0131, FR0011, FR0033, FR0026 and FR0132 read past harmless attributes. FR0118 leaves shared and detached work, comparisons and overloads with another return type alone; FR0152 ignores unrelated removals.

 0.8.47: FR0066 resolves a query text&apos;s names to the binding in scope and folds constants (holes, `+`, sprintf and String.Format of constants, `Module.name`), read where the text was built: a per-member `let baseQuery = "..."` is no finding. Loaded code (an analyzer, source generator, MSBuild task or a driver&apos;s finalizer) crashing on a background thread no longer ends the run: reported once, the run goes on and exits 1; out of memory and the tool&apos;s own failures still stop it.

 0.8.46: FR0182 checks a lambda&apos;s pattern parameter against the lambda&apos;s body and stays quiet where the scope holds an `#if`. A test file is also recognised by a qualified or non-first test attribute; FR0092 finds a C# test pinning a failure message and leaves the message alone.</PackageReleaseNotes>
    <Authors>Tuomas Hietanen</Authors>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/Thorium/fsharp-refactor</PackageProjectUrl>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/Thorium/fsharp-refactor</RepositoryUrl>
    <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
    <PackageTags>fsharp;dotnet-tool;analyzers;refactoring;codefix;static-analysis;code-quality;linter;code-cleanup;sarif;mcp;mcp-server;ai;llm;agents</PackageTags>
    <PackageIcon>icon.png</PackageIcon>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <PackageLicenseExpression>Unlicense</PackageLicenseExpression>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="..\..\README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
    <None Include="..\..\icon.png" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <Compile Include="FileWalk.fs" />
    <Compile Include="Workspace.fs" />
    <Compile Include="Program.fs" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Update="FSharp.Core" Version="10.1.201" />
    <!-- FSharp.Analyzers.SDK drags in 6.0.0, which is OLDER than the 8.0.0.0 a
         SQLProvider type provider asks for: its MySqlConnector fails to
         initialise against ours and the whole project reports as broken.
         Pinned forward so the provider's own reference resolves. -->
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Logging.Abstractions" Version="8.0.0" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\FSharp.Refactor.Analyzers\FSharp.Refactor.Analyzers.fsproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
